# Packages an image installs on top of the Ubuntu 26.04 base (P14 ISO installer; F-images reuses this list read-only).
# One package per line. vrx-meta pulls everything else — the agent, the API, the web front end, our VPP build at the
# exact manifest version and every daemon the renderers drive (deploy/debian/vrx/debian/control) — so nothing that
# vrx-meta already depends on is listed here (the P10 rule). APT Recommends stay ON, exactly like
# scripts/10-install-runtime.sh, so that the ISO and the package path produce the same box (D-202 (1)).
vrx-meta
